/// Send one message, spinning while the ring is full, and give
/// up after a deadline.
///
/// # Parameters
///
/// - `self`: this producer, by shared reference, so one handle
///   may be used from several threads at once.
/// - `give_up`: how long to keep trying while the ring is full,
///   counted from the first attempt that finds it full.
///   `Micros(0)` makes one attempt and returns.
///   [`Micros::FOREVER`] never gives up.
/// - `fill`: called once with a mutable reference to the claimed
///   slot's message, to write the message in place. Not called
///   when the send returns `Err(Full)`.
///
/// # Type parameters
///
/// - `T`: the message type. Its size must be at most the slot
///   size less [`SLOT_HEADER_BYTES`](super::SLOT_HEADER_BYTES),
///   and its alignment at most `SLOT_HEADER_BYTES`, or the send
///   panics.
///
/// # Returns
///
/// - `Ok(())`: the message is written and committed, and the
///   consumer can read it.
/// - `Err(Full)`: the ring stayed full until `give_up` passed.
///   Nothing was written.
///
/// # Notes
///
/// - Needs the `std` feature, which provides the clock.
/// - The clock is read only once the ring is found full, so a
///   send that finds room reads no clock.
/// - Losing a slot to another producer is not a full ring: the
///   send retries at once.
/// - A consumer asleep on an empty ring is woken after the
///   commit.
/// - If `fill` panics, the slot stays claimed and is never
///   committed, and the consumer waits at it until the ring is
///   restarted.
#[cfg(feature = "std")]
pub fn send_with_x<T>(&self, give_up: Micros, fill: impl FnOnce(&mut T)) -> Result<(), Full>

